#!/bin/bash
# Weekly Uptime Kuma update (homelab, 2026-11-15). Kuma runs from a git checkout
# (/opt/uptime-kuma-src, owned by user kuma) with data in /opt/uptime-kuma/data.
# Moves to the newest stable 2.x tag, following upstream's non-Docker steps
# (git checkout <tag>; npm ci --omit dev; npm run download-dist). Backs up kuma.db
# first and restores tag + DB if the UI doesn't come back.
set -uo pipefail
export LC_ALL=C
SRC=/opt/uptime-kuma-src; DATA=/opt/uptime-kuma/data; BK=/opt/uptime-kuma/update-backups
note() { /usr/local/sbin/homelab-notify "$*"; echo "$*"; }
k() { runuser -u kuma -- env HOME=/var/tmp/kuma-home npm_config_cache=/var/tmp/kuma-home/.npm "$@"; }
mkdir -p /var/tmp/kuma-home && chown kuma:kuma /var/tmp/kuma-home
cd "$SRC" || exit 1

cur=$(k git describe --tags --exact-match 2>/dev/null) || { note "kuma auto-update: checkout is not on a release tag, not touching it"; exit 1; }
k git fetch --tags -q || { note "kuma auto-update: git fetch failed"; exit 1; }
latest=$(k git tag -l '2.*' | grep -E '^2\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$' | sort -V | tail -1)
[ -n "$latest" ] || exit 1
if [ "$cur" = "$latest" ]; then echo "uptime-kuma $cur is current"; exit 0; fi

install_tag() {
  k git checkout -q --force "$1" && k npm ci --omit=dev --no-audit --no-fund --loglevel=error && k npm run -s download-dist
}
up() {
  for _ in $(seq 36); do
    sleep 5
    c=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -m 5 http://127.0.0.1:3001/)
    [[ "$c" =~ ^(200|302)$ ]] && systemctl is-active -q uptime-kuma && return 0
  done
  return 1
}

systemctl stop uptime-kuma
rm -rf "$BK/$cur"; mkdir -p "$BK/$cur"; chmod 700 "$BK"
cp -a "$DATA"/kuma.db* "$BK/$cur/" || { systemctl start uptime-kuma; note "kuma auto-update: DB backup failed, aborted"; exit 1; }

if install_tag "$latest"; then
  systemctl start uptime-kuma
  if up; then
    ls -1t "$BK" | tail -n +4 | while read -r d; do rm -rf "$BK/$d"; done
    note "uptime-kuma auto-update OK: $cur -> $latest (DB backup in $BK/$cur)"
    exit 0
  fi
fi

# roll back
systemctl stop uptime-kuma
install_tag "$cur"
cp -a "$BK/$cur"/kuma.db* "$DATA/"
systemctl start uptime-kuma
if up; then st="healthy again"; else st="STILL DOWN, needs attention now"; fi
note "uptime-kuma auto-update $cur -> $latest FAILED; ROLLED BACK to $cur ($st)"
exit 1
